# Victory Suite (`vs-*`)

Making robots badly in rust.

This is a Cargo workspace. All first-party crates live under `libs/` and share the
`vs-` prefix (short for **Victory Suite**).

## Structure

```
libs/
  vs-wtf        Core time primitives (Timepoint, Timespan, Timecode)
  vs-data-store  In-memory datastore + bucketed primitives + topics + serde
  vs-broker     Broker / commander node system on top of the datastore
```

## Crates

### vs-wtf
The time library. Provides `Timepoint`, `Timespan`, and `Timecode` primitives with
lossless conversions between unit scales.

### vs-data-store
The datastore. Bucketed, typed primitives with a topic/key model, retention,
serialization (`rmp-serde`, `bincode`), and a TCP listener. Exposes a CLI (`main`)
and benchmarks (`divan`).

### vs-broker
The broker. Builds on `vs-data-store` + `vs-wtf` to provide a broker node,
commanders, task definitions, and TCP/channel adapters. Ships two binaries:
`broker_tcp_server` and `broker_tcp_client`.

## Building

```sh
cargo build
cargo test
```

## Version bumps / dependency updates

External dependency version bumps are applied crate-by-crate. Changes stay
minimal (version string only where possible) and any behavioural risk is called
out in code comments plus `OPEN_RISKS.md`.
